    <string name="section_autolock">Auto lock the Mac</string>
    <string name="autolock_switch">Lock the Mac when I walk away</string>
    <string name="autolock_explanation">While the clipboard sync is on, the phone broadcasts a short Bluetooth signal every quarter of a second. The Mac averages its strength and locks its screen once the average says you have left, which also means the Mac needs this switched on in its own menu. Nothing is scanned and nothing is connected to; the signal carries no data beyond a token derived from the pairing code.</string>
    <string name="autolock_needs_sync">Turn the clipboard sync on: the beacon only broadcasts while it is running.</string>
    <string name="autolock_needs_permission">Grant Nearby devices below, otherwise the phone cannot broadcast.</string>
